Z||000014||Black88GT||07-10-2000||12:42 PM||||The Car and Driver article was meant to offer an UNBIASED viewpoint.  Yes, as Fiero lovers we can sit here all day and talk about how "great" the car is, but mags like that help because they don't own the cars daily or generally care about them so they are HONEST.  AS I SAID IN MY LAST POST I DIDNT MEAN ANY FLAMES.  I understand some people are jealous (yes I said it) they can't find a good deal on an 88, but I didn't mean to incite a riot here with those people.  The 88s I found for that cheap needed work, true.  They were by no means "rough".  Just because a car is in CT doesn't mean the frame is rusted out.  But even with all the work they needed, it was STILL worth it.  All I am trying to say is that stock for stock the '88 is the best year fiero, HANDS DOWN, no comparison, don't even try to debate it.  And yes, you can buy your brakes from the local autoparts store, but sometime down the road when parts for ALL fiero's get hard to find, you better hope places like the Fiero store still exist.<BR>If people (i.e. cheap fiero owners) would support them now they WILL exist.  Unless the difference in price is huge I generally will buy from them.  Hell I couldn't find upper ball joints anywhere else.  If it wasn't for them I would be up shits creek without a paddle! I guess only non-off the shelf part non- X-car '88 owners can appreciate that... <P><BR>jeff||||reg||12
Z||000015||Black88GT||07-10-2000||12:47 PM||||Oh I missed something.  Now he is saying "in a sunny state" Jesus why don't we go all out and say in a sunny state garage kept under 100k miles new clutch on a street with no other Fiero's! FYI, that Formula was purchased in FLORIDA (ask him), he found it when he was going to buy an original '88 coupe t-top for 1,000, I forgot about that one.  As I said it is pretty solid, I would want it but its an automatic, just my personal preference is a 5 speed.  The cars I have found were in Maryland, where there are 4 seasons.  The best of both worlds I guess you could say.  Buy no means did they have any rust on them except for the battery tray which I heard happens a lot.<P>no flaming,<BR>jeff<BR>  ||||reg||1
Z||000016||ChadMan||07-10-2000||12:51 PM||||Newfie,<P>The 88 Coupe does indeed have the same suspension and upgraded brakes as the 88 GT and Formula - except the Coupe has softer springs and no rear antisway bar.  It does handle rough pavement better than the 84-87, but handling on smooth pavement isn't noticeably better IMHO.  The 88 brakes are much better than earlier versions (11" vented rotors vs 9.7" solid rotors).<P>It's easy to tell an 88 Coupe from an 84-86 as the front and rear fascia are different (84-86 had black bumper pads, 87-88 did not).  It's harder to tell an 88 from an 87, but here are four ways to tell them apart:<P>1) Twin cutouts for exhaust in the rear fascia.  87's only had one cutout; 88's had two because Pontiac used the same fascia on the Formula V6.<BR>2) Different seat fabric.  88's used the same traditional Pontiac cloth (little diamonds) - 87's had a slightly different weave (little rectangles).<BR>3) Front track - The 88 suspension has a wider front track and the front wheels protrude slightly from the fenders.<BR>4) Rear suspension - crawl under there and have a looksee.  88's will have long, thin trailing arms that run longitudinally and have a big bolthead facing the rear of the car on either side.<P>I have an 88 Coupe and I love it.  But brake and suspension parts really are pricier than 84-87 and are harder to find.||||reg||1
Z||000017||stimpy||07-10-2000||08:02 PM||||Yo Black,<P>I said in a sunny state cuz I live in one. Not to be picky. And I do believe that FL would have good deals cuz they sold a buttload of Fieros there new. Likewise CA. I happen to live in truck country (OK) where Fieros are somewhat rare, with even a high mile rebuild 85 GT commanding $2g. While I think it's great you hooked up a deal, you gotta admit those are ore exception then rule.<P>And if ya think I'm consumed with jealousy, you can kees ma azz!<P>No flame intended.  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://gifs123.tripod.com/page15/renstimpy2.gif"> ||||reg||1
